I wouldn't be so confident. Defamation is an issue for the Civil Law (not 
criminal), thus cases are assessed on "balance of probabilities" not
"beyond reasonable doubt". Also the presumption would be that the message
was passed unaltered unless you could show (at least suggestive) evidence
that it was not what you wrote. It might come down to whether or not a
judge (or perhaps jury) believed your word.

